## 🛠️ Technology Stack

### Frontend
- **Next.js 13+** - React framework with App Router
- **React 18** - UI library
- **TypeScript** - Type-safe development
- **Tailwind CSS** - Utility-first CSS framework
- **shadcn/ui** - High-quality, accessible UI components
- **React Hook Form** - Efficient form handling
- **SWR/React Query** - Data fetching (based on hooks)

### Backend Services
- **Supabase** - Backend as a service (authentication, database)
- **REST API** - Custom API routes in Next.js

### Development Tools
- **ESLint** - Code quality
- **TypeScript** - Type safety
- **Next.js Middleware** - Route protection & authentication

## 🔐 Authentication & Authorization

The application uses a **middleware-based authentication system**:

```typescript
// src/middleware.ts
- Checks for valid auth token
- Protects customer, seller, and admin routes
- Allows public access to home, products, login, and register
- Redirects unauthorized users to login page
```

### User Roles
- **Customer** - Browse products, make purchases, view orders
- **Seller** - Manage products, view sales, track orders
- **Admin** - (Future) System administration

## 🎯 Key Features

### ✅ Implemented
- Product Browsing - Browse and search products
- Shopping Cart - Add/remove items, manage quantities
- Checkout - Multi-step checkout process
- Order Management - Track orders, view history
- User Profiles - Customer and seller profiles
- Seller Dashboard - Product and order management
- Responsive Design - Mobile-friendly interface
- Authentication - Secure login/registration

### 📋 In Progress/Planned
- Wishlist - Save favorite products
- Ratings & Reviews - Product reviews
- Payment Integration - Stripe or similar
- Admin Panel - System management
- Email Notifications - Order updates
- Advanced Analytics - Seller insights

## 🚀 Deployment

### Vercel (Recommended)
The easiest way to deploy a Next.js application:

1. Push your code to a Git repository (GitHub, GitLab, etc.)
2. Connect your repository to [Vercel](https://vercel.com)
3. Vercel automatically builds and deploys on push
4. Configure environment variables in Vercel dashboard

### Other Platforms
- **Docker** - Containerize the application
- **AWS** - EC2, Lambda, or Amplify
- **Azure** - App Service or Container Instances
- **DigitalOcean** - App Platform or Droplets

